  "id": "contact-comfort",
  "term": "contact comfort",
  "definition": "Contact comfort is the soothing effect of simple physical closeness or touch from another person, such as handholding. In this context, it can lessen perceived threat and help regulate negative emotional reactions, especially when the relationship is close and supportive.",
